# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will find the root cause of your JavaScript or Node.js bug and fix it
category: Programming & Tech
subcategory: Debugging
tags:
  - bug fix
  - node.js
  - javascript
  - debugging
  - error fix
description: >-
  Stuck on a bug, a crash or an error log that makes no sense? I find the real cause, not just the
  line that failed, and fix it so it stays fixed.


  My daily work is reading production logs from a large multi-system project and tracing each
  failure to its source. Every fix comes with a test, so the same bug cannot come back silently.


  What I fix:

  - Crashes, errors and unhandled promises in Node.js and JavaScript

  - Electron app problems (windows, IPC, packaging)

  - Scripts that worked yesterday and fail today

  - Slow or stuck processes and memory leaks


  What you get:

  - A short explanation of what was wrong and why

  - The fix, as a clear change you can review

  - A test that fails before the fix and passes after


  How it works: send the error, the log and how to reproduce it. I reply with what I find before I
  change anything.
packages:
  basic:
    name: One Bug
    description: Root cause and fix for one bug, with a short explanation.
    deliveryDays: 1
    revisions: 1
    price: 35
  standard:
    name: Bug and Test
    description: Root cause, fix and a test that keeps it fixed.
    deliveryDays: 3
    revisions: 2
    price: 90
  premium:
    name: Stability Pass
    description: Up to 5 related bugs, fixes, tests and a short report.
    deliveryDays: 6
    revisions: 3
    price: 220
faq:
  - question: What do you need?
    answer: >-
      The error message, the log, and the steps that make it happen. Access to the code, as a zip or
      a repository.
  - question: What if you cannot find it?
    answer: >-
      I tell you what I found and what I ruled out, and we agree the next step. You are not charged
      for a guess.
  - question: Will you change other code?
    answer: Only what the fix needs. Anything else I notice is listed for you to decide.
requirements:
  - Paste the error message and describe what you were doing when it happened.
  - Who will use it, and on what? (Windows, Mac, a server; one person or a team)
  - What must it always do, and what must it never do?
  - How will you check that it is done? (the test you will run, or what you will look at)
  - Please share any files, examples, access or data I need to start.
